  "text": "משקיע\nביקור\n\nמשקיע\n\nמשקיע \n\nTo solve the problem, let's break it down into smaller steps:\n\n1. **Understanding the Structure:**\n   - A regular hexagon has 6 vertices.\n   - Each vertex is connected to the midpoint of its opposite side.\n\n2. **Determining the Intersection:**\n   - The intersections occur where two lines (one connecting vertices of one pair and one connecting vertices of another pair) intersect.\n   - These intersections form angles based on the directions of the lines.\n\n3. **Identifying Acute Angles:**\n   - Acute angles are those less than 90 degrees.\n   - For a regular hexagon, when connecting vertices with each other or with the midpoints of the opposite sides, we expect certain angles to be acute due to symmetry.\n\n4. **Counting Acute Angles:**\n   - We need to count how many of these intersections result in acute angles.\n   - By symmetry and logical deduction, we find that certain configurations of lines in a regular hexagon will create acute angles.\n\n5. **Final Count:**\n   - After considering all possible combinations, we determine that the maximum number of acute angles formed by the intersection of two line segments is 7.\n\nThus, the maximum number of acute angles is \\boxed{7}.",
